 "hand_coded_findings": [
  {
   "finding_id": "F-001-245073-01",
   "case_id": "001-245073",
   "ordinal": 1,
   "article": "P1-1",
   "family": "QUALIFIED",
   "outcome": "violation",
   "decisive_limb": "QR-NECESSITY",
   "paragraph_no": 104,
   "verified_verdicts": {
    "QR-LEGALITY": "not_examined",
    "QR-NECESSITY": "failed"
   },
   "why": "Para 82 expressly leaves the issue of lawfulness open and para 86 states that fair balance is the remaining question; para 104 concludes the fair balance was not ensured. The Registry keyword line names an imprecise legal framework, which is not a holding that the interference was unlawful."
  },
  {
   "finding_id": "F-001-234522-01",
   "case_id": "001-234522",
   "ordinal": 1,
   "article": "2",
   "family": "LIFE",
   "outcome": "violation",
   "decisive_limb": "A2-PROC",
   "paragraph_no": 52,
   "verified_verdicts": {
    "A2-PROC": "failed",
    "A2-SUB": "not_examined"
   },
   "why": "Para 52 holds the investigative authority failed to explore all credible lines of inquiry; para 53 states the violation is under the procedural limb. The substantive obligation was not examined."
  },
  {
   "finding_id": "F-001-236179-01",
   "case_id": "001-236179",
   "ordinal": 1,
   "article": "8",
   "family": "QUALIFIED",
   "outcome": "violation",
   "decisive_limb": "QR-POSITIVE",
   "paragraph_no": 91,
   "verified_verdicts": {
    "QR-POSITIVE": "failed",
    "QR-LEGALITY": "not_examined",
    "QR-AIM": "not_examined"
   },
   "why": "Paras 89-90 assess what the authorities failed to do to facilitate reunification and para 91 concludes the applicant did not receive effective protection of her family life. The case is never analysed as an interference, so the legality, aim and necessity limbs are not reached."
  },
  {
   "finding_id": "F-001-242957-01",
   "case_id": "001-242957",
   "ordinal": 1,
   "article": "8",
   "family": "QUALIFIED",
   "outcome": "violation",
   "decisive_limb": "QR-NECESSITY",
   "paragraph_no": 77,
   "verified_verdicts": {
    "QR-NECESSITY": "failed",
    "QR-LEGALITY": "satisfied",
    "QR-AIM": "satisfied"
   },
   "why": "Para 66 establishes that terminating parental authority was an interference and para 60 records it as in accordance with the law and pursuing a legitimate aim; para 77 concludes insufficient weight was attached to the family life. Positive-duty reasoning inside an interference analysis does not make this a positive-obligation case."
  },
  {
   "finding_id": "F-001-233686-01",
   "case_id": "001-233686",
   "ordinal": 1,
   "article": "8",
   "family": "QUALIFIED",
   "outcome": "no_violation",
   "decisive_limb": "QR-NECESSITY",
   "paragraph_no": 104,
   "verified_verdicts": {
    "QR-NECESSITY": "satisfied"
   },
   "why": "Para 104 holds the authorities gave sufficient consideration to the applicant's family ties and carried out the balancing without overstepping the margin of appreciation; para 105 finds no violation."
  },
  {
   "finding_id": "F-001-245254-01",
   "case_id": "001-245254",
   "ordinal": 1,
   "article": "5",
   "family": "LIBERTY",
   "outcome": "violation",
   "decisive_limb": "A5-GROUNDS",
   "paragraph_no": 150,
   "verified_verdicts": {
    "A5-GROUNDS": "failed"
   },
   "why": "The Court found the detention was not based on a reasonable suspicion for the purposes of Article 5 s 1 (c), which para 150 restates. The permitted-grounds limb is the one reached first and it decides the finding."
  },
  {
   "finding_id": "F-001-245254-02",
   "case_id": "001-245254",
   "ordinal": 2,
   "article": "10",
   "family": "QUALIFIED",
   "outcome": "violation",
   "decisive_limb": "QR-LEGALITY",
   "paragraph_no": 152,
   "verified_verdicts": {
    "QR-LEGALITY": "failed"
   },
   "why": "Para 152 holds the interference cannot be justified under Article 10 s 2 since it was not prescribed by law. This is the contrast case to 001-245073: here the Court decides lawfulness rather than leaving it open, so necessity is never reached."
  },
  {
   "finding_id": "F-001-245254-03",
   "case_id": "001-245254",
   "ordinal": 3,
   "article": "18",
   "family": "MISUSE",
   "outcome": "violation",
   "decisive_limb": "A18-PURPOSE",
   "paragraph_no": 173,
   "verified_verdicts": {
    "A18-PURPOSE": "failed"
   },
   "why": "Para 173 finds it proven beyond reasonable doubt that the detention pursued the ulterior purpose of stifling pluralism; para 175 holds the violation of Article 18 in conjunction with Article 5 s 1."
  },
  {
   "finding_id": "F-001-242639-01",
   "case_id": "001-242639",
   "ordinal": 1,
   "article": "3",
   "family": "ILLTREATMENT",
   "outcome": "no_violation",
   "decisive_limb": "A3-SUB",
   "paragraph_no": 115,
   "verified_verdicts": {
    "A3-SUB": "satisfied"
   },
   "why": "The first Article 3 finding concerns medical treatment in detention. Para 110 holds the underestimation of the illness did not result in a lack of treatment reaching the Article 3 threshold and para 115 finds the continued detention did not constitute inhuman or degrading treatment. This is the substantive obligation answered in the State's favour."
  },
  {
   "finding_id": "F-001-242639-02",
   "case_id": "001-242639",
   "ordinal": 2,
   "article": "3",
   "family": "ILLTREATMENT",
   "outcome": "violation",
   "decisive_limb": "A3-SUB",
   "paragraph_no": 147,
   "verified_verdicts": {
    "A3-SUB": "failed"
   },
   "why": "The second Article 3 finding concerns the section 41 bis regime. Para 145 records that the authorities never considered lifting or easing the additional restrictions despite explicit requests, and para 147 finds a violation in respect of that part of the complaint. One judgment carrying both a no-violation and a violation finding on the same article is why findings are keyed by their order in the operative provisions."
  },
  {
   "finding_id": "F-001-242203-01",
   "case_id": "001-242203",
   "ordinal": 1,
   "article": "6",
   "family": "FAIRTRIAL",
   "outcome": "no_violation",
   "decisive_limb": "A6-DEFENCE",
   "paragraph_no": 71,
   "verified_verdicts": {
    "A6-DEFENCE": "satisfied"
   },
   "why": "The complaint is that no adjustment measures were made for the applicant's cognitive impairment, which goes to his ability to participate in his own defence. Para 69 records that he never substantiated any specific impact on the fairness of the trial and para 71 concludes the proceedings taken as a whole were fair for the purposes of Article 6 s 1 and s 3."
  },
  {
   "finding_id": "F-001-243562-01",
   "case_id": "001-243562",
   "ordinal": 1,
   "article": "14",
   "family": "DISCRIMINATION",
   "outcome": "no_violation",
   "decisive_limb": "A14-DIFFERENCE",
   "paragraph_no": 96,
   "verified_verdicts": {
    "A14-DIFFERENCE": "satisfied"
   },
   "why": "Para 96 finds nothing in the material to support the contention that the applicant was deprived of custody on the basis of his disability alone, so no difference in treatment on the prohibited ground is established; para 98 concludes there was no violation of Article 14 in conjunction with Article 8."
  },
  {
   "finding_id": "F-001-233111-01",
   "case_id": "001-233111",
   "ordinal": 1,
   "article": "P1-3",
   "family": "ELECTIONS",
   "outcome": "violation",
   "decisive_limb": "P13-CONDITIONS",
   "paragraph_no": 106,
   "verified_verdicts": {
    "P13-CONDITIONS": "failed"
   },
   "why": "The Court applies the Mugemangango test to the Althingi credentials procedure; para 91 records that its conclusion on the first step in principle obviates the need to assess the other two, and para 106 holds there has been a violation in respect of both applicants."
  },
  {
